  "prefLabel": "Ed 1128.03 Limitations on Reimbursement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1128.03 Limitations on Reimbursement. A responsible school district shall:\n\n(a) Be eligible for reimbursement only for those direct costs which are included in the IEP of a child with a disability, and which qualify as special education and related services; and\n\n(b) Not be reimbursed for:\n\n(1) Costs which exceed rates established by Ed 1129 for tuition, instruction, room and board, and related services; or\n\n(2) Indirect costs.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17; ss by #12601, eff 8-9-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
